## Context

Ticket 0057 built the base-vs-census comparison pipeline: tabulate and
plot scripts, Makefile wiring, auto-regeneration from wildcards. PR #238
merged with n=9 models. The table footnote flags this as underpowered.

The census arm has 37 models. The p1_base arm has 9. Running the
remaining 28 models under p1_base will produce a properly powered
comparison.

## Current p1_base models (9)

deepseek-v3.2, gemini-2.5-flash-lite, gemini-3-flash-preview, kimi-k2.5,
minimax-m2.7, mistral-small-2603, qwen3.5-122b-a10b, qwen3.5-35b-a3b,
seed-2.0-lite

## Missing (28)

All other census models: claude-opus-4.6, claude-sonnet-4.6, devstral-small-2,
gemma4:{31b,e2b,e4b}, glm-4.7-flash, glm-5-turbo, gpt-5-mini, gpt-5-nano,
gpt-5.4, grok-4.20, llama-4-maverick, mercury-2, mistral-large-2512,
mistral-small3.2, mimo-v2-{flash,pro}, nemotron-3-nano (x2),
qwen3.5-{2b,4b,9b,35b,397b-a17b,plus-02-15}, qwen3.6-plus-preview,
step-3.5-flash

## Actions

1. Batch cloud models through the parametric ablation harness with
   prompt=p1_base, repeat=2-3
2. Batch local models (qwen3.5:2b/4b/9b/35b) on Padme via query_rag
   analog or direct parametric call — serial, one Ollama job at a time
3. `make tables figures` to regenerate tab_base_vs_census.tex and
   fig_base_vs_census.pdf

## Test

```bash
make report/inputs/generated/tab_base_vs_census.tex
# Verify model count increased from 9
```

## Exit criteria

- p1_base records exist for all 37 census models (or documented reason
  for exclusion)
- Table and figure regenerated with full intersection
- Footnote "underpowered" removed or updated
